<title>POLAND: NBP drains PLN 394 mln from Polish money market.</title>
<headline>NBP drains PLN 394 mln from Polish money market.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland drained 394 million zlotys from the market through a reverse NBP-bill repurchase auction after banks bid to place 603 million with the central bank, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The bank drained the market for seven days at a maximum rate of 22.89 percent, just down from Thursday's maximum of 22.90 percent. The average rate rose to 22.85 from 22.52.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 2 653 9700</p>
</text>
